Z||000000||formula2||07-13-2001||10:25 PM||||Hi I am from montreal Quebec. Just bought a "new" 86 Fiero GT.<BR>We do not have fiero store of any kind here..<BR>Is there any national store in the US , lets say in the Burlington Vermont area where i can get some parts??????<BR>I know about fierostore.com. Is it reliable???<P>Pontiac Grand Prix GT 1997<BR>Pontiac Fiero GT 1986..||||reg||5
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-13-2001||11:14 PM||||The Fiero Store is great. I use them all the time, and so do quite a few other people in the forum. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||07-14-2001||12:04 AM||||There are a lot of great parts vendors available to you. Since the advent of the internet and mail order you can choose any vendor you want. Click the 'Fiero Parts Vendors' button at the top of the screen for a good list. Depending on what you need Rodney Dickman, Paul McKibben, Fiero Warehouse, Fiero Dave, Chris Pond, mrfiero... these are some of the best. Some deal in new stuff, some deal in used. Never be afraid to ask for recommendations here before you buy anything... We are all in this together...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||07-14-2001||10:28 AM||||First, welcome to the forum!<P>The Fiero store is great! I have had no problems with them and they are fast.<P>There are some shops in Canada too.<BR>There's a Fiero shop in Canada.(Weston,Ont.) <A HREF="http://www.thefieroshop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroshop.com</A> <P>There's also Fiero Conversions Inc.<BR>(Windsor, Ont.) (519)-972-4989 <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||14
